{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"f2d639f3-8b0e-436a-a8bf-e2fca4e8240b\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What does Article 37 say about direct enforcement of the Directive Principles?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 37 नीति निदेशक तत्वों के सीधे प्रवर्तन के बारे में क्या कहता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Only the Supreme Court may enforce them\",\"hi\":\"केवल सर्वोच्च न्यायालय उन्हें लागू करा सकता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only High Courts may enforce them\",\"hi\":\"केवल उच्च न्यायालय उन्हें लागू करा सकते हैं\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Parliament may enforce them without a law\",\"hi\":\"संसद बिना कानून के उन्हें लागू करा सकती है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"They are not enforceable by any court\",\"hi\":\"वे किसी भी न्यायालय द्वारा प्रवर्तनीय नहीं हैं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Meaning of DPSP\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/359f70a69695affb9d72f8393102bd2e.pdf#page=99\",\"citation\":\"Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Exploring Society: India and Beyond, Grade 7 Part 1 — The Constitution of India: An Introduction\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/gees110.pdf#page=13\",\"citation\":\"Chapter 10, PDF p. 13: DPSP are government goals/guidelines and cannot by themselves be claimed before a judge; contrast with Fundamental Rights\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"constitution_partiv: Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38 | ncert_nonjusticiable_p13: Chapter 10, PDF p. 13: DPSP are government goals/guidelines and cannot by themselves be claimed before a judge; contrast with Fundamental Rights\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ed9bb5ed-b4a8-4004-8844-73018fc7b99b\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Consider the following statements about Article 37:\\n1. Directive Principles are not enforceable by any court.\\n2. They are fundamental in the governance of the country.\\n3. The State has a duty to apply them in making laws.\\nWhich of the statements are correct?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 37 के संबंध में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:\\n1. नीति निदेशक तत्व किसी न्यायालय द्वारा प्रवर्तनीय नहीं हैं।\\n2. वे देश के शासन में मूलभूत हैं।\\n3. कानून बनाते समय उन्हें लागू करना राज्य का कर्तव्य है।\\nकौन-से कथन सही हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"1 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"1 and 2 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1 और 2\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"2 and 3 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 2 और 3\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"1, 2 and 3\",\"hi\":\"1, 2 और 3\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Meaning of DPSP\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/359f70a69695affb9d72f8393102bd2e.pdf#page=99\",\"citation\":\"Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"constitution_partiv: Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e0283128-0208-4c56-8897-6941f83ea115\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Why are Directive Principles often described as “positive” obligations?\",\"hi\":\"नीति निदेशक तत्वों को प्रायः “सकारात्मक” दायित्व क्यों कहा जाता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"They prohibit every form of State action\",\"hi\":\"वे राज्य की हर कार्रवाई पर रोक लगाते हैं\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"They apply only after a court order\",\"hi\":\"वे केवल न्यायालय के आदेश के बाद लागू होते हैं\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"They require the State to take steps toward constitutional goals\",\"hi\":\"वे राज्य से संवैधानिक लक्ष्यों की दिशा में कदम उठाने की अपेक्षा करते हैं\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"They automatically punish citizens\",\"hi\":\"वे नागरिकों को स्वतः दंडित करते हैं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Meaning of DPSP\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/359f70a69695affb9d72f8393102bd2e.pdf#page=99\",\"citation\":\"Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Political Science (317), Lesson 7 — Directive Principles of State Policy and Fundamental Duties\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://www.nios.ac.in/media/documents/srsec317newE/Learner_guide_eng/317_LG_E_L7.pdf#page=3\",\"citation\":\"Learner’s Guide p. 3: DPSP are positive, non-justiciable, aim at social-economic democracy, complement Fundamental Rights, and require legislation for implementation\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"constitution_partiv: Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38 | nios_l7_p3: Learner’s Guide p. 3: DPSP are positive, non-justiciable, aim at social-economic democracy, complement Fundamental Rights, and require legislation for implementation\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"dfb9056e-dff7-4035-aced-3c4738257547\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which statement correctly distinguishes Directive Principles from Fundamental Duties?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सा कथन नीति निदेशक तत्वों को मौलिक कर्तव्यों से सही रूप में अलग करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Both are addressed only to courts\",\"hi\":\"दोनों केवल न्यायालयों को संबोधित हैं\"