p. 1: Part IV guidelines to Union/State governments, Irish influence, law and policy for collective good, and citizen duties\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"constitution_partiv: Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38 | ncert_vision_p12: Chapter 10, PDF pp. 12–13: DPSP as social-economic vision, governance goals and guidelines | nios_l7_p1: Learner’s Guide p. 1: Part IV guidelines to Union/State governments, Irish influence, law and policy for collective good, and citizen duties\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d7df8f98-d5fd-4878-93e9-833788bdcae3\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which Article defines the term “State” for Part IV of the Constitution?\",\"hi\":\"संविधान के भाग IV के लिए “राज्य” शब्द को कौन-सा अनुच्छेद परिभाषित करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 12\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 12\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 32\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 32\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 37\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 37\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 36\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 36\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Meaning of DPSP\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/359f70a69695affb9d72f8393102bd2e.pdf#page=99\",\"citation\":\"Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/359f70a69695affb9d72f8393102bd2e.pdf#page=69\",\"citation\":\"Official PDF p. 69: Part III heading and Article 12 definition of “the State”\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"constitution_partiv: Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38 | constitution_partiii_art12: Official PDF p. 69: Part III heading and Article 12 definition of “the State”\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"cb6ee06e-9de2-4cf7-8e9b-a4c2f03446c8\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"When a Directive Principle is implemented by a valid statute, what is the immediate source of legal enforceability?\",\"hi\":\"जब किसी नीति निदेशक तत्व को वैध अधिनियम द्वारा लागू किया जाता है, तो कानूनी प्रवर्तनीयता का तात्कालिक स्रोत क्या होता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The implementing statute and its legal provisions\",\"hi\":\"क्रियान्वयन अधिनियम और उसके कानूनी प्रावधान\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 37 alone, without any law\",\"hi\":\"बिना किसी कानून के केवल अनुच्छेद 37\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A political speech\",\"hi\":\"राजनीतिक भाषण\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The Irish Constitution directly\",\"hi\":\"सीधे आयरिश संविधान\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Meaning of DPSP\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/359f70a69695affb9d72f8393102bd2e.pdf#page=99\",\"citation\":\"Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Political Science (317), Lesson 7 — Directive Principles of State Policy and Fundamental Duties\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://www.nios.ac.in/media/documents/srsec317newE/Learner_guide_eng/317_LG_E_L7.pdf#page=3\",\"citation\":\"Learner’s Guide p. 3: DPSP are positive, non-justiciable, aim at social-economic democracy, complement Fundamental Rights, and require legislation for implementation\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"constitution_partiv: Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38 | nios_l7_p3: Learner’s Guide p. 3: DPSP are positive, non-justiciable, aim at social-economic democracy, complement Fundamental Rights, and require legislation for implementation\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c4d68a90-5087-49f6-b2d0-b02881fe2896\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"When constitutional text permits more than one plausible reading, how may the Directive Principles be used?\",\"hi\":\"जब संवैधानिक पाठ के एक से अधिक युक्तिसंगत अर्थ संभव हों, तब नीति निदेशक तत्वों का उपयोग कैसे किया जा सकता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"To replace the written text with any preferred policy\",\"hi\":\"लिखित पाठ को किसी भी पसंदीदा नीति से बदलने के लिए\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"To make every Directive Principle directly enforceable\",\"hi\":\"हर नीति निदेशक तत्व को सीधे प्रवर्तनीय बनाने के लिए\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"As an interpretive aid for a harmonious reading, without rewriting an express right\",\"hi\":\"किसी स्पष्ट अधिकार को दोबारा लिखे बिना सामंजस्यपूर्ण व्याख्या में सहायक के रूप में\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"To remove the need for legislative competence\",\"hi\":\"विधायी क्षमता की आवश्यकता समाप्त करने के लिए\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Meaning of DPSP\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Property Owners Association v. State of Maharashtra, 2024 INSC 835\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/1992/78629/78629_1992_1_1501_57003_Judgement_05-Nov-2024.pdf#page=132\",\"citation\":\"Paras 143–147, PDF pp. 132–134: harmonious interpretation, relevance of DPSP, rights-conflict limit and legislative competence\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/359f70a69695affb9d72f8393102bd2e.pdf#page=99\",\"citation\":\"Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"sc_interpretation_p132: Paras 143–147, PDF pp. 132–134: harmonious interpretation, relevance of DPSP, rights-conflict limit and legislative competence | constitution_partiv: Official PDF p. 99: Part IV heading and Articles 36–38\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"b0d90255-48a2-48c3-bef7-12147f14ab25\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A law claims to advance a Directive Principle. What follows for judicial review?\",\"hi\":\"कोई कानून किसी नीति निदेशक तत्व को आगे बढ़ाने का दावा करता है। न्यायिक समीक्षा के लिए इसका क्या परिणाम है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The law automatically becomes a constitutional amendment\",\"hi\":\"कानून स्वतः संविधान संशोधन बन जाता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Every Fundamental Right challenge must be dismissed without examination\",\"hi\":\"हर मौलिक अधिकार चुनौती बिना जांच खारिज करनी होगी\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The claim alone creates no complete immunity; relevant constitutional review still applies\",\"hi\":\"केवल यह दावा पूर्ण प्रतिरक्षा नहीं देता; प्रासंगिक संवैधानिक समीक्षा फिर भी लागू होती है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 37 prevents courts from examining any implementing law\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 37 न्यायालयों को किसी भी क्रियान्वयन कानून की जांच से रोकता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Meaning of DPSP\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Property Owners Association v. State of Maharashtra, 2024 INSC 835\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/1992/78629/78629_1992_1_1501_57003_Judgement_05-Nov-2024.pdf#page=133\",\"citation\":\"Paras 144–145, PDF pp. 133–134: DPSP in reasonableness review; no clear rights conflict and legislative competence limitations\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"http